| Slice | [GMEOW Affect Module](../../slices/affect/index.md) |

![completeness: Docs 11/17](../../badges/completeness/11.svg) ![stability: stable](../../badges/stability/stable.svg) ![category: Class](../../badges/category/class.svg) ![box: TBox](../../badges/box/boxtbox.svg) ![stereotype: Kind](../../badges/stereotype/kind.svg)

## Definition

The declared reference frame a numeric affect reading is expressed against: its range \(gmeow:profileRangeMin/gmeow:profileRangeMax\), midpoint \(gmeow:profileMidpoint\), polarity \(gmeow:profilePolarity — bipolar/unipolar\), and normalization transform \(gmeow:profileTransform\)\. A magnitude on an affect axis is meaningless without one \(Principle 11: a value asserted without its frame is ill\-formed\)\. Scale arithmetic — normalization, cross\-scale conversion, and the metric under which magnitudes combine into an intensity — is solver work outside the logic \(Principle 12\); the profile DECLARES the frame, it does not compute in triples\. The affect\-domain analogue of the rubrics facility's gmeow:ScoreScale: a distinct declared frame for a numeric affect reading, not a rubric's judging scale, so the two axes stay separately identified\.

